.TH ERASE_FILE 3ggl "11 August 1997" "GGL/IGP ETHZ" "GGL Common Lib"
.SH NAME
erase_file \- enhanced file removal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <common/inout.h>

.RB "int " erase_file
.RI "(FILE *" filename ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The function
.B erase_file()
will erase the file
.I filename
when it exists. It is an extension to
.BR unlink (2)
by additionally printing a proper error message, when a file could not
be removed or be found. 
.SH "RETURN VALUES"
.B erase_file()
will return the error code, that it received by calling
.BR unlink (2).
.SH ERRORS
The function will call standard library functions
that may set
.IR errno .
If any called function produces an error, the functions
will print an appropriate error message to
.BR stderr .
.SH CAVEATS
You have to compile your program using
.I -lcommon
as a compiler flag to properly link
your function to the library.
